Look up Parallel Axis Theorem.<br><br>Such as <a href="http://scienceworld.wolfram.com/physics/ParallelAxisTheorem.html" class="postlink">here</a>, or <a href="http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/parax.html" class="postlink">here</a>. You can then use this to calculate your combined moments of inertia from the separate bodies as if they are point masses at the new combined centre of mass.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=60">dog</a> — Thu Feb 23, 2006 7:45 pm</p><hr />
